# Copy to .env and fill in. All optional — the site builds without them.

# Public iCal feed URL(s) for the parish calendar — comma- or newline-separated.
# Any provider works: ChurchDesk (Calendar → share/subscribe), Google Calendar
# ("Secret address in iCal format"), Outlook, anything publishing RFC 5545.
# webcal:// addresses are accepted and rewritten to https://.
# When set, events are pulled at build time and merged with the `events`
# collection on /whats-on and in /calendar.ics; if unset, the collection is used
# on its own. A feed that is missing or unreachable only logs a warning — it can
# never fail a deploy. Add a daily deploy hook so build-time events stay fresh.
# EVENTS_ICAL_URLS=

# Legacy name for the same thing, still honoured. Prefer EVENTS_ICAL_URLS above.
# CHURCHDESK_ICAL_URL=

# Plausible Analytics domain (privacy-friendly, cookieless). When set, the
# Plausible script is emitted on every page. Leave unset to ship no analytics tag.
# PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=barnabites.org
